# LeakSanitizer suppressions for scripts/asan-slice.sh (RFC-0016 S8ck-r, INF-04).
#
# Rules. Every entry names a frame outside nelli (nim-z3, libz3). A frame
# under src/nelli is never suppressed; a leak there is fixed at its root
# (nelli's per-thread state included: releaseSymexThreadState,
# src/nelli/thread_state.nim). Each entry carries its source and the
# condition that retires it. LSan treats what a suppressed object references
# as suppressed too, so an entry for a leaked context also covers the libz3
# memory the context owns.
#
# No entries. The last one, `leak:context::newContext` (nim-z3's FuncDecl,
# FuncInterp and RcfNum hooks never released their `ctx`, INF-04 item 2),
# retired with the milpa.lock bump to nim-z3 d86efda, which releases it.
